 ## 6. Conclusion

-Offering two LLM sellers a private channel left a trace that an overseer could see, but not the one we set out to find. The channel showed up as a higher price level. Co-movement detectors that work on scripted colluders found no robust contemporaneous co-movement, and public messages gave an LLM auditor no resolved gain. Because high prices also arise without any channel, a model-matched price-level screen is a good trigger for a deeper audit, not evidence of an agreement on its own. The key open test is whether deliberately evasive colluders can keep their prices inside the matched reference while still coordinating.
+Offering two LLM sellers a private channel left a trace that an overseer could see, but not the one we set out to find. The channel showed up as a higher price level. We detected no robust contemporaneous pCMI signal across the main designs; lagged transfer entropy was above chance in the grid. Public messages gave an LLM auditor no resolved gain. Because high prices also arise without any channel, a model-matched price-level screen is a good trigger for a deeper audit, not evidence of an agreement on its own. The key open test is whether deliberately evasive colluders can keep their prices inside the matched reference while still coordinating.

